Crow v1.2.1.2: client address for requests rejected at URL time (phto: structured access log).

Stock Crow sets request::remote_ip_address in handle_header()/handle(). A request whose URL matches no
route is answered with a 404 from handle_url(), i.e. while the request line is being parsed and before
either runs, so those requests reach the middleware's after_handle with an empty address. This patch sets
the address at the start of handle_url(), so it is known for every request.

For such unmatched-route requests the rest of the request is not parsed yet: X-Forwarded-For and
X-Request-Id are not available (the client address is the direct peer, a request id is generated), and
the middleware's before_handle does not run (duration is reported as 0).

diff --git a/include/crow/http_connection.h b/include/crow/http_connection.h
--- a/include/crow/http_connection.h
+++ b/include/crow/http_connection.h
@@ -108,6 +108,7 @@
         void handle_url()
         {
+            req_.remote_ip_address = adaptor_.remote_endpoint().address().to_string();
             routing_handle_result_ = handler_->handle_initial(req_, res);
             // if no route is found for the request method, return the response without parsing or processing anything further.
             if (!routing_handle_result_->rule_index)
